# promise: #539
# A screenshot app's "window under the pointer" over a Little Window takes the Little Window, over
# its strip and its page alike. Screenshot apps that list windows through ScreenCaptureKit (iShot
# on macOS 27) see no sharing state or alpha, so on the engine they took the never-seen window
# holding the profile's pages, laid over whichever Cra window was in use, the Little Window
# included, and the shot came out blank (GitHub #539, 0.1.48; the browser window's side is #346).
# The readout reads the window list the way such a picker does (cra://debug?screenshotPick).
budget rss=700 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
pace 0.5

cra://action/newLittleWindow
wait 1
cra://debug?littleCard=go:${PAGE}?n=little-pick
wait 2
cra://debug?littleShown=page
expect-log little shown page: windows=1 .* card=0
cra://debug?screenshotPick=200,12&target=little
expect-log screenshot pick at 200,12: little window
cra://debug?screenshotPick=200,200&target=little
expect-log screenshot pick at 200,200: little window
cra://debug?screenshotPick=700,450&target=little
expect-log screenshot pick at 700,450: little window

# The browser window behind it too, once it is the window in use again.
cra://action/newWindow
wait 2
cra://debug?screenshotPick=150,400
expect-log screenshot pick at 150,400: main window
reject-log fault:
